      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That radiating, heavy feeling wrapping toward your side and stomach is a sign that you need to take this seriously; it could be more than just a simple muscle cramp. Taking a high, unprescribed dose of ibuprofen like 1000mg is dangerous and can cause serious stomach issues. Instead, try applying heat *after* the initial ice period, and focus on gentle core engagement exercises if the pain allows. If the pain is spreading or accompanied by any digestive changes, you should stop self-treating and seek medical advice.",
